From 3b988a1ce486b62a44b4beb7cba1ebafc68230fb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arena Agent <agent@arena.ai>
Date: Sun, 16 Aug 2026 22:34:21 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/6] i686 -Os size: ESP-slot peepholes, store-to-load
 forwarding, scratch-copy propagation, if-convert at -Os

The kernel real-mode setup (arch/x86/boot, -m16 -Os) overflowed its
hard 64-sector limit: lccc's setup .text was ~48K vs GCC's ~17K. The
oracle comparison (lccc vs GCC -Os on the extracted number()/printf
reproducer) shows the fat is one pattern family: the i686 codegen
round-trips nearly every IR value through a stack slot and funnels
every copy through %eax. Four measures, each byte-measured on the
reproducer (1048 -> 791 bytes; GCC = 312):

1) if_convert now also runs at -Os (was skipped): the branchy select
   lowering emits two arms full of slot round-trips, strictly bigger
   than the setcc/cmov form. Measured: -Os without if-conversion was
   LARGER than -O2 with it (1156 vs 955). GCC if-converts at -Os too.

2) ESP-relative slots participate in ALL slot peepholes. With
   -fomit-frame-pointer (implied by -Os and the boot Makefile) every
   local lives at N(%esp), but the peephole classifier only matched
   (%ebp) - the entire slot-optimization tier was a dead letter for
   real-mode code. (%esp) slots get a disjoint offset namespace
   (ESP_SLOT_BIAS) so they can never be confused with (%ebp) slots.
   SOUNDNESS: push/pop and any instruction writing %esp are now
   barriers - an ESP adjustment renumbers every (%esp) slot, so no
   slot window may cross one. Pushes/pops only occur at prologue/
   epilogue and around calls (calls were already barriers).

3) forward_slot_loads: window-scan store-to-load forwarding. After
   `movl %R, N(%esp)`, a later exact reload becomes `movl %R, %R2`
   (or a NOP when R2==R); once every reload is forwarded, the
   existing never-read-store elimination deletes the store itself.
   Stops at barriers, overlapping stores/loads, writes to %R,
   indirect memory, folded-operand slot accesses, and implicit
   register writers (mul/div/cltd/string ops).

4) Scratch-copy propagation: `movl %SRC, %T; movl %T, X` where %T is
   dead after the consumer (bounded written-before-read scan) becomes
   a single `movl %SRC, X` - the i686 codegen emits this %eax-funnel
   shape for nearly every assignment. Plus load+move fusion:
   `movl SLOT, %eax; movl %eax, %REG` -> `movl SLOT, %REG` under the
   same deadness proof.

Validation: 685 lib / 192 regression / 50 correctness green;
differential fuzz 240/240 (O2+Os, seeds 0:120) - the fuzzer runs Os
now exercising all new peepholes end-to-end.
