From 3dbc41e4e36aec3861f468fec9ef5ee126b0adca Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arena Agent <agent@arena.ai>
Date: Sun, 16 Aug 2026 23:02:08 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/6] asm: `.` in .set expressions is label-valued
 (post-layout), fix SYM_FUNC_END sizes

The kernel's SYM_FUNC_END expands to
  .set .L__sym_size_X, .-X ; .size X, .L__sym_size_X

Two bugs made every such size wrong or zero:

1) SizeExpr::SymbolRef never consulted the new set_values table, so all
   sizes evaluated through the .set constant fold silently became 0.
   objtool then mis-decoded retpoline.o ("can't find jump dest
   instruction at .text..__x86.return_thunk+0xc0": with
